@@ -2,6 +2,14 @@
 
 ## Unreleased
 
+- Derive Genesis host time from integer step counts and a per-environment restored origin. Single-step and batched calls now agree at scoring-window boundaries; selected resets, playback and device-to-host barriers rebase the affected clocks. The separate device tensor clock retains its existing precision.
+
+- Preserve explicit inertial values at FP64 precision in the Genesis portable XML handoff; compiled XML rounding no longer silently changes these parameters. Implicit inertials remain native-inferred.
+
+- Genesis factory calls reject unprefixed options that were silently overwritten; use `genesis_friction_cone` (and the corresponding prefixed solver options) with `create_backend`, or constructor names with `GenesisBackend` directly. Initial reports expose the requested and effective native friction-cone names.
+
+- Added an optional detached rigid-contact snapshot contract with explicit state, collision and force epochs, public geometry identities, per-contact force orientation and independently read body net forces. Genesis 1.4.3 mapped rigid scenes expose the candidate readback; other adapters and older Genesis releases remain unsupported for this complete snapshot. Added explicit Genesis CPU/FP64/seed/determinism selection, actuated armature and noslip overrides, plus initial effective native configuration reports. The default Genesis extra remains 1.3.3; unqualified 1.4.3 mass/COM randomization fails closed. See the bilingual contact-readback documentation for the runtime qualification boundary.
+
 - Moved MotrixSim packed host-bridge sensor layout validation off the step/reset hot path (unilabsim/UniLab#2102). `MotrixHostBridgeTransferPlan` previously re-read every physical sensor through `SceneModel.get_sensor_value` on each full and selected packed read to re-check widths; the full layout contract check now runs only at compile time, while hot reads re-verify only the plan-owned staging buffer shapes. A Motrix scene layout is immutable for the lifetime of its backend and `MotrixBackend.close()` closes every compiled plan fail closed, so explicit layout drift still fails closed at compile/open and backend teardown.
 
 ## 1.7.12 - 2026-10-08
